[FINAL-TEXT] The startup script is definitive. The comment reads: `# Mode: On (static) -> Linux Bond Mode 0 (Balance-RR)` — this is the translation error. Cisco's "EtherChannel mode on" (static, XOR-based load balancing) was wrongly mapped to Linux `bond mode 0` (round-robin). PC1 can reach its gateway via simple ICMP, but TCP flows reorder severely across the two alternating physical links, causing the periodic "blinks."

